@startsalt
' Screen: Org-Wide Schedule List
' User Stories:
'   - As an admin, I can see all schedules across the organization at a glance
'   - As an admin, I can enable or disable individual schedules inline
'   - As a developer, I can see when each schedule will next fire
'   - As an admin, I can create a new schedule from this page

{
  <b>codefre.sh</b> | Dashboard | Scripts | Prompts | Agents | <b>Schedules</b> | Settings
  ==
  {
    <b>Schedules</b>
    ..
    {
      "Search schedules...                   " | Script: ^All Scripts^  | Status: ^All^  | [+ New Schedule]
    }
    ==
    {#
      <b>Schedule Name</b>         | <b>Script</b>               | <b>Agent</b>          | <b>Cron</b>       | <b>Timezone</b>  | <b>Next Run</b>              | <b>Enabled</b>     | <b>Actions</b>
      nightly-code-audit     | nightly-code-audit    | gpt4o-primary   | 0 3 * * *   | UTC        | 2026-05-13 03:00 UTC    | [X] On            | [Edit] [Run Now]
      weekly-dep-scan        | dep-scan              | claude-opus-prod | 0 9 * * 1  | UTC        | 2026-05-18 09:00 UTC    | [X] On            | [Edit] [Run Now]
      ci-pr-gate             | ci-gate-check         | gpt4o-primary   | */15 * * * * | UTC      | 2026-05-12 09:30 UTC    | [] Off            | [Edit] [Run Now]
    }
    ..
    {
      3 schedules total  |  <color:green>2 enabled</color>  <color:gray>1 disabled</color>
      ..
      <i>All times shown in UTC. Adjust timezone per-schedule in the edit form.</i>
    }
  }
}
@endsalt
